      The most prevalent design flaw in residential sprinkler systems is placing sprinkler heads so that their spray streams barely touch tip-to-tip. Due to gravitational trajectory and water atomization, individual sprinkler heads apply less water the farther out droplets travel. To achieve uniform turf hydration without brown rings or soggy swamps, you must design around <strong>100% head-to-head overlap</strong> and balance <strong>Matched Precipitation Rates (MPR)</strong> across every zone.
    </p>

