        description: "Confusing radius (center to edge) with diameter (edge to edge) leads homeowners to place 15-foot spray heads 30 feet apart, leaving massive dry patches between every head.",
        solution: "Remember that head-to-head spacing means the physical distance between Head 1 and Head 2 must equal the rated throw radius of the nozzle (e.g., 15 ft throw = 15 ft spacing)."
